---
<p>TypeScript adds types to a running language; Bayan starts with them. Unions, narrowing, <code>switch</code>, <code>strict</code> mode and <code>null</code> only where the type allows will look right. Bayan builds a native program with no runtime: sized integers, owned memory, and a wrong type stops the build instead of being erased.</p>
<p>Every program ran with the compiler; the output is real.</p>

